    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can create personalized learning paths, explaining concepts in simple language. They can generate practice problems tailored to a student’s level and provide instant feedback. For example, an LLM could help a student visualize a calculus problem through step-by-step animations, making abstract ideas more tangible."
